    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">There are a few problems I can see. <div><br></div><div>(1)</div><div>Maybe I don’t understand the big picture of your model, but the order of calculations seems weird. I’m assuming X1 and Y are data; a and b are parameters. You should probably have this line</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187)\"><code><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">LogitP</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>i<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> a <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span> b<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">*</span>X1<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>i<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">);</span></code></div></div></div></blockquote><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div>before this one</div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187)\"><code>P<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>i<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span> inv_logit<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">LogitP</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span>i<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">));</span></code></div></div></div></blockquote>you might not even need this second one (see next comment).</div><div><br></div><div><font face=\"Roboto, sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(249,250,252)\">(2)</span></font></div><div><font face=\"Roboto, sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(249,250,252)\">This line seems strange </span></font><span style=\"font-family:monospace\">Y_hat</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace\">i</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace\"> max</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Type</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace\"> min</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Type</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">),</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace\">P</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace\">i</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)));</span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(249,250,252)\"><font face=\"Roboto, sans-serif\">Shouldn’t P(i) always be between 0 and 1? If so, won’t this calculation always make </font></span><span style=\"font-family:monospace\">Y_hat</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace\">i</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)=</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace\">P</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace\">i</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)?</span></div><div><font face=\"Roboto, sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(249,250,252)\">If there is a reason to do this in the model, there’s still a risk that using max and min will cause discontinuities in the likelihood surface.</span></font></div><div><font face=\"Roboto, sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(249,250,252)\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"Roboto, sans-serif\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(249,250,252)\">(3)<br></span></font><div>dbinom_robust takes these arguments</div><div>dbinom_robust<span style=\"font-family:Roboto,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(249,250,252)\">(Type k, Type size, Type logit_p, int give_log=0)</span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(249,250,252);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif\">In the case of Bernoulli data, size =1, but you’ll need to use Type(1).)</span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(249,250,252);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(249,250,252);font-family:Roboto,sans-serif\">Maybe you just need</span></div></div></div>"
